WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Plot three plus two i
on an Argand diagram.

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.460
Multiply it by i.

3
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.560
You land on minus two plus three i.

4
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.940
Again: minus three minus two i.

5
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.900
Again: two minus three i.

6
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.540
Once more, and you're
back where you started.

7
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.390
Every step is a quarter-turn
round the origin,

8
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.180
ninety degrees, at the same distance.

9
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.100
Why?

10
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.100
Does multiplying by i just swap the parts?

11
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.600
Is it a reflection?

12
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.550
In this mission, you'll describe a
point by a distance and an angle:

13
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.730
its modulus and its argument.

14
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.140
You'll write complex numbers
in polar and Euler form,

15
00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.180
r e to the i theta.

16
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.480
Then you'll find out what multiplying
does to the modulus and argument.

17
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:50.050
Your mission: explain why multiplying
by i rotates a point by ninety degrees.
